TODO STATE
================================================================================

INPUT STATE:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

inputValue

Example:

"Buy milk"


LIST STATE:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

todos

Example:

[
  {
    id: '...',
    text: 'Buy milk',
    completed: false,
    createdAt: Date
  }
]


================================================================================
ADDING TO AN ARRAY
================================================================================

DO NOT:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

todos.push(
  newTodo
)


Instead create a new array:

setTodos(previousTodos => [

  ...previousTodos,

  newTodo

])


Before:

[
  todo1,
  todo2
]


After:

[
  todo1,
  todo2,
  newTodo
]


================================================================================
WHY USE A FUNCTIONAL SETTER?
================================================================================

The new array depends on the existing array.

Therefore:

setTodos(previousTodos => [
  ...previousTodos,
  newTodo
])


is a strong update pattern.


MEMORY:

NEXT STATE DEPENDS ON PREVIOUS STATE
            ↓
USE FUNCTIONAL SETTER


================================================================================
WHY USE crypto.randomUUID()?
================================================================================

List items need stable identifiers.

A generated UUID gives each newly created item its own identity.

Example:

{
  id: crypto.randomUUID(),
  text: 'Buy milk'
}


Then render:

<li key={todo.id}>


IMPORTANT:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Date.now() is convenient for demos, but a timestamp is not a robust guarantee
of uniqueness.

In production applications, IDs often come from:

• Backend/database identifiers

• crypto.randomUUID()

• Another intentional ID-generation strategy


