PART 9: ADVANCED FORM-TO-LIST FEATURES
================================================================================

FEATURE 1: SORTING
================================================================================

If you only need a sorted VIEW, you often don't need to mutate/rewrite the
original items array.


Example:

const sortedItems = [

  ...items

].sort((a, b) =>

  a.name.localeCompare(
    b.name
  )

)


IMPORTANT:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Array.prototype.sort() mutates the array it is called on.

Therefore don't do:

items.sort(...)


on React state directly.

Copy first:

[...items].sort(...)


================================================================================
FEATURE 2: FILTERING
================================================================================

Suppose:

const [filter, setFilter] =
  useState('all')


Derive what should be displayed:

const visibleItems =
  filter === 'all'
    ? items
    : items.filter(
        item =>
          item.category ===
          filter
      )


You usually do NOT need a separate:

filteredItems

state if it can be calculated from:

items + filter


================================================================================
FEATURE 3: SEARCH
================================================================================

const [query, setQuery] =
  useState('')


const visibleItems =
  items.filter(item =>

    item.text
      .toLowerCase()
      .includes(
        query
          .trim()
          .toLowerCase()
      )

  )


Again:

SEARCH RESULTS ARE DERIVED DATA.


Store:

items
+
query


Derive:

visibleItems


